\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Measured transition temperature $\ensuremath  {T_{\mathrm  {c}}}$ vs ideal temperature $\ensuremath  {{T_{\mathrm  {c}}^{\mathrm  {ideal}}}}= \ensuremath  {T_{\mathrm  {c}}}(1 + \setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle \xi $}\mathaccent "0362{\xi })$. The dashed line indicates $\ensuremath  {{T_{\mathrm  {c}}^{\mathrm  {ideal}}}}= \ensuremath  {T_{\mathrm  {c}}}$. Most materials lie close to the identity, with a subset receiving larger upward corrections due to structural noise. }}{6}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
